OL,3,GNEWSAMan's conviction for murdering
OL,4,Awoman to be reviewed
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man who was jailed along with his
OL,7,Fbrother for murdering a woman after she
OL,8,Freported homophobic abuse by some of
OL,9,Ftheir associates is to have his
OL,10,Fconviction reviewed.
OL,12,FNicholas Curtis was jailed for a
OL,13,Fminimum of 18 years alongside Stuart
OL,14,FCurtis following the death of
OL,15,F44-year-old Glenda Jackson in
OL,16,FBirkenhead in 2018.
OL,18,FThe Criminal Cases Review Commission
OL,19,F(CCRC) has Nicholas Curtis's partial
OL,20,Fdefence of loss of control was not
OL,21,Fproperly considered at his trial or put
OL,22,Fbefore the jury.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
